    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The accusative: what you have",
     "texto": [
      "The thing that receives the action of the verb goes in the **accusative**. The good news: only the **masculine** changes. **Ein** becomes **einen**: **Ich habe einen Bruder** (I have a brother).",
      "The feminine and neuter don't change: **eine Schwester**, **ein Kind**.",
      "To say you don't have something, use **kein**, which changes in the same way: **Ich habe keinen Bruder**, **Ich habe keine Schwester**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Nominative and accusative",
     "columnas": [
      {
       "texto": "",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Masculine",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Feminine",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Neuter",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      }
     ],
     "filas": [
      [
       {
        "texto": "subject (nominative)",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
