       },
       {
        "texto": "kein Kind",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       }
      ]
     ],
     "nota": "",
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "My, your, our and your (plural)",
     "texto": [
      "**Mein** (my) and **dein** (your) change like «ein»: **mein Vater**, **meine Mutter**, **meine Eltern** (plural). **Unser** (our) and **euer** (your, plural) follow the same pattern: **unser Bruder**, **unsere Schwester**, **unsere Eltern**; **euer Vater**, **eure Mutter**. The form **euer** loses an «e» when it takes the ending: **eure**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
